Applied to triton-ext 1afa671b (head of triton-ext#142) by
docker/rocm-triton-ext.Dockerfile.

The PR targets Triton main, where AsyncCopyGlobalToLocalOp takes a cachePolicy
attribute. On release/3.8 the op takes cache/evict/isVolatile/contiguity
instead, and their defaults are what the PR passes on main.

Release/3.8 also has no TritonSemantic.make_tensor, so uTLX falls back to
patching tl.tensor.__init__ process-wide. _promote then re-types every gluon
distributed_type (a block_type subclass whose IR always carries an encoding)
as a plain carrier, and every gluon kernel in the process -- e.g. aiter's
mla_gluon decode -- fails with "expected ... to be a distributed_type".
Gluon values already carry their layout, so _promote leaves them alone.

On AMD the add_stages hook also replaced the ttgir stage of every kernel,
gluon included, with the uTLX TTIR->TTGIR pipeline; that conversion marks
gluon's amdg.buffer_load_to_local illegal. The hook now leaves non-Triton
languages on their own stages.

